{
 "title": "Why fast bullets go through walls",
 "captions": [
  {
   "text": "This bullet just went !through! a wall.",
   "hide": true,
   "s": 0.15,
   "e": 1.907,
   "se": 1.587
  },
  {
   "text": "The wall was *fine.*",
   "s": 1.907,
   "e": 3.179,
   "se": 2.859
  },
  {
   "text": "Games don't move objects !smoothly.!",
   "s": 3.179,
   "e": 5.116,
   "se": 4.796
  },
  {
   "text": "They jump them forward *once per frame,* then check for collisions.",
   "s": 5.116,
   "e": 8.659,
   "se": 8.34
  },
  {
   "text": "A slow object always lands *touching* the wall.",
   "s": 8.659,
   "e": 11.428,
   "se": 11.108
  },
  {
   "text": "But a !fast! bullet can be in front of the wall",
   "s": 11.428,
   "e": 13.443,
   "se": 13.123
  },
  {
   "text": "on one frame and already !behind it! on the next.",
   "s": 13.443,
   "e": 16.202,
   "se": 15.882
  },
  {
   "text": "The check never sees it touching. It's called !tunnelling.!",
   "say": "The check never sees it touching. It's called tunneling.",
   "s": 16.202,
   "e": 19.139,
   "se": 18.819
  },
  {
   "text": "The fix: *sweep* the bullet's whole path between frames",
   "s": 19.139,
   "e": 22.017,
   "se": 21.697
  },
  {
   "text": "and find where it would *hit.*",
   "s": 22.017,
   "e": 23.447,
   "se": 23.127
  },
  {
   "text": "Engines call it *continuous collision detection.*",
   "s": 23.447,
   "e": 26.062,
   "se": 25.742
  },
  {
   "text": "Follow: tomorrow, AI doesn't see letters.",
   "say": "Follow. Tomorrow: A.I. doesn't see letters.",
   "s": 26.062,
   "e": 28.198,
   "se": 28.198
  }
 ],
